<title>USA: Dow Jones average gains more than 100 points.</title>
<headline>Dow Jones average gains more than 100 points.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow Jones industrial average rose more than 100 points in late trading Friday, spurred by news that the White House and congressional Republican leaders agreed on a plan to balance the U.S. federal budget by 2002.</p>
<p>Just after 3:48 p.m EDT, the Dow was up 100.74 points at 7,077.22.</p>
